<title>MALAYSIA: Sungei, Reliance debt upgraded.</title>
<headline>Sungei, Reliance debt upgraded.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Debt issues of five Malaysian companies including Sungei Way Holdings Bhd and Reliance Pacific Bhd, were upgraded to AA3 from A1, said the Rating Agency Malaysia (RAM) on Friday.</p>
<p>RAM said the upgrades were made after the long-term debt of their guarantor bank, RHB Sakura Merchant Banker Bhd had been upgraded.</p>
<p>Gamuda Bhd, Ipmuda Bhd and Sumway Building Technology Bhd were also upgraded to AA3 from A1, said RAM</p>
<p>&quot;As a result of (RHB Sakura's) upgrade, the ratings for the (other) companies debt issue have been upgraded to reflect the strength of the bank guarantor,&quot; said RAM.</p>
